  "tileDescription": "{id, select, meadow{Extensive grassland. Cheap, decent habitat, cools a little.} cropland{Farmland. Low habitat value, small CO2 source.} forest{Deciduous forest. Best habitat, absorbs CO2, dampens noise and dust. Matures over decades.} water{Pond or lake. Good habitat, cools its surroundings.} park{Urban park. Recreation within 300 m, cooling, some habitat.} housing_low{Single-family homes, about 45 residents per hectare.} housing_high{Apartment blocks, about 180 residents per hectare with ground-floor services.} commercial{Offices and shops. Jobs, shopping within walking distance, delivery noise.} industry{Manufacturing. Many jobs, noise, emissions.} road{Main road. Connects housing to jobs; traffic causes noise and pollution.} wetland{Reeds and shallow water. The richest habitat here, cools strongly, and soaks up runoff from its surroundings.}solar_field{Ground-mounted panels on open grassland. Displaces a great deal of power-station CO2; dark, fenced and not a place people go.}mixed_use{Homes above shops and workshops. Fewer flats than apartment blocks, but work and shopping are already downstairs.}school{Classrooms, a yard and a sports field. Expensive to build and to run, brings jobs, and is empty at night.}tram_stop{A stop with its track. Quieter than the road traffic it stands in for, and electric, so nothing is burnt here.}cycle_path{A surfaced path through a planted verge. Cheap, nearly silent, and keeps most of the ground open.}other{}}",
