  "indicatorFormula": "{id, select, biodiversity{Biotope values (BKompV) times maturity, reduced by threats from roads, industry and buildings and by fragmentation, then scaled with a species-area curve.} air{Emissions from traffic, industry and buildings spread with an exp(-d/300 m) kernel, vegetation removes part, and the resident-weighted mean becomes the score.} noise{Every source loses 20 dB per distance decade and forest or buildings attenuate further; each resident scores (65 dB - L) / 10, clamped to 0-1.} housing{100 x min(1, capacity / (jobs / 0.52)) x (0.5 + 0.5 x occupancy); zero without housing.} economy{100 x (0.6 x min(1, jobs / workers) + 0.4 x budget trend), the trend taken from the budget change in the last month.} shopping{Huff model with lambda = 2 over shops within 700 m walking distance, averaged over the residents.} recreation{Resident-weighted 0.7 x green space within 300 m plus 0.3 x (1 - delta T / maximum urban heat).} commuting{100 x (0.5 x (1 - mean distance / 20 km) + 0.5 x (1 - car share)) from the gravity commute model.} climate{100 x (0.7 x (1 - CO2 per person / 5.0 t) + 0.3 x (1 - mean delta T / maximum urban heat)).} flood{100 x (1 - mean runoff / design storm). Runoff per cell is the SCS curve-number method on the cell's sealed fraction; water and wetland subtract from their neighbours first.} budget{The municipal budget divided by the starting budget, clamped to 0-100.} other{}}",
