  "missionBeatBody": "{id, select, village_first_homes{People live here now. Turn on the shopping overlay to see which homes can reach a shop on foot, and which cannot.}village_quiet_left{Look at what is still meadow and forest. A village that reaches everything but keeps nothing quiet has only solved half the task.}noise_first_homes{Open the noise overlay. The band along the road is loud whatever you build there—distance is doing most of the work.}noise_shield{Quiet is slipping. Try putting forest or a park between the road and the homes, and watch the overlay rather than the score.}habitat_two_patches{Both forests count as habitat, but biodiversity also asks whether animals can move between them. Check the connectivity figure.}habitat_maturity{New forest is not yet old forest. Let months pass and watch biodiversity climb without you placing anything.}budget_monthly{The balance still looks healthy because it started high. The monthly figure is the one that decides whether this lasts.}budget_delay{What you built months ago is only now showing up in the budget. Expect the same lag from what you build today.}quarter_first_block{Homes, work and shopping in the same walkable area are what keep commutes short. Check the commuting indicator as you go.}quarter_balance{Some goals are met. The remaining ones usually cost something the met ones gave you—decide what you are willing to trade.}other{Look at what changed on the map before you build again.}}",
